# Critical vulnerabilities of the reference image that the trivy jobs of
# ci.yml and nightly.yml accept for now (see the policy in the Dockerfile).
# Only an unfixed one, in a package the tests cannot do without, may be
# listed, as two or more lines:
#
#   # <package>: why the vulnerability does not reach the conversion of
#   # untrusted images, and the Ubuntu tracker link
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# The expiry is at most 30 days after the entry is added: Trivy stops
# ignoring the vulnerability that day, the scan fails again, and the entry
# is reviewed (removed once the fix ships, renewed with a new reason).
#
# No entries: the scan of 2026-11-01 reported no critical vulnerability,
# fixed or not.
